  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "As the episode begins, Max philosophizes about life, destiny, and the choices we make, while Chef Viktor Barinov is already busy shouting orders at his suppliers.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Считают, что человек – хозяин судьбы.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы сами всё решаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы решаем, с кем нам быть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Всё зависит только от нас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но судьба преподносит нам сюрприз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Когда мы начинаем в это верить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она делает это обычно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Хорошо, Тимур.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Привези мне мясо ягнёнка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Молодого ягнёнка, а не пенсионера.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Не как вчера.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Вчера было плохое мясо.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's listen to their conversation.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Считают, что человек – хозяин судьбы.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'They say we are masters of our fate.' The question word for 'what' comes right at the start, followed directly by 'fate'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы сами всё решаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We decide everything ourselves.' Max puts 'we' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'yourselves'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы решаем, с кем нам быть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We decide who we want to be with.' The key word here means 'we', which Max combines with 'decide'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Всё зависит только от нас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Everything depends only on us.' Here 'depends' sets up the idea, while 'us' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но судьба преподносит нам сюрприз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But fate brings us a surprise.' The key word here means 'fate', which Max combines with 'present'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Когда мы начинаем в это верить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'When we start believing in this.' Max starts with 'when' and pairs it with 'we' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она делает это обычно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It usually does this.' Listen for the word meaning 'it' right alongside 'does' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Хорошо, Тимур.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'All right, Timur.' In Russian, 'good' leads into 'Timur' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Привези мне мясо ягнёнка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Bring me some lamb meat.' A compact expression built around 'to bring' and 'lamb'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Молодого ягнёнка, а не пенсионера.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'A young lamb, not a pensioner.' A compact expression built around 'young' and 'pensioner'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Не как вчера.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Not like yesterday.' A compact expression built around 'how' and 'yesterday'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Вчера было плохое мясо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yesterday the meat was bad.' Chef Viktor puts 'yesterday' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'was'. Now let's hear the whole thing once more.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
